{
  "title": "APD receiver — avalanche gain & excess noise",
  "group": "Links & receivers",
  "description": "APD photodiode + TIA link. Sweep the APD gain M to see the receiver sensitivity optimum: SNR improves with M while thermal-limited, then degrades once the M^2 F(M) excess noise dominates.",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -96,
        "title": "APD receiver — avalanche gain vs excess noise",
        "lines": [
          "Same OOK link as the photodiode+TIA example, but the receiver is an",
          "AVALANCHE photodiode (APD1). Its internal gain M multiplies the",
          "primary photocurrent R*P by M, so vout ~= -M*R*P*TIA1.gain_ohm — the",
          "recovered swing scales directly with M.",
          "",
          "But multiplication amplifies shot noise SUPER-linearly: the McIntyre",
          "excess factor F(M) = k*M + (2 - 1/M)(1 - k) makes the shot-noise PSD",
          "2q*Iprim*M^2*F(M). Run with noise seeds on and sweep M = 1, 5, 10,",
          "20, 40 (APD1.M): the noise on vout grows faster than the signal past",
          "the noise-optimal M* (here ~10), so the eye first opens then closes.",
          "That thermal-limited -> excess-noise-limited crossover is the whole",
          "point of an APD receiver.",
          "",
          "k_ion (ionization ratio) sets how fast F(M) grows: k=0.1-0.3",
          "(InP/InGaAs) is far quieter at high M than k~1 (symmetric ionization)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "instances": {
